.nh
.TH "PB-LOGIN" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-login - Sign in through browser approval on any device


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb login [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Sign in through browser approval on any device

.PP
Alias for pb auth login. Print an approval link and sign in through WorkOS on any device, including when this machine has no browser. Credentials stay on the requesting CLI and installation or machine ownership is unchanged.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--change-account\fP[=false]
	sign in with another account after browser approval

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for login

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print approval and sign-in states as JSON

.PP
\fB--no-browser\fP[=false]
	print the approval link without opening a browser

.PP
\fB--reauth\fP[=false]
	authenticate the current account again


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb(1)\fP
